# ti.msp432p401r.freertos_demo
# Real, hand-written (no vendor SDK/generator - see target.toml) FreeRTOS
# (CMSIS-RTOS v1) demo for TI MSP432P401R - this chip's genuine Cortex-M4F
# core, so the real ARM_CM4F FreeRTOS port applies, reused verbatim from
# tm4c123/freertos_demo's own already-proven bundle. See
# ../../../../../replica-server/renoly_examples/ti/msp432p401r/README.md.

using sysbus
mach create "MSP432P401R_FreeRTOS_Demo"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platform.repl

# Bare @$ORIGIN/firmware.elf - REQUIRED, not stylistic, same real reason
# as every other demo's sim.resc in this repo (see blink_uart_demo's own
# sim.resc for the full incident writeup).
sysbus LoadELF @$ORIGIN/firmware.elf

# EUSCI_A0 TXBUF write watchpoint - observes uartTask's marker/heartbeat
# bytes. is_byte_tap -> Bus Traffic, matching every other UART example.
sysbus AddWatchpointHook 0x4000100E 4 Write "print(chr(value & 0xFF), end='')"

# DIO Port A OUT-register write watchpoint, masked to the real P1.0 bit -
# register-level proof defaultTask's blink loop genuinely toggles the
# pin. Not a byte-tap -> lands as a real, labeled [DIO] Event.
sysbus AddWatchpointHook 0x40004C02 4 Write "print('[DIO] P1.0 write value=0x%X' % (value & 0x1))"

# EUSCI_B0 TXBUF write watchpoint - real, register-level proof spiTask
# genuinely drives the SPI self-loopback (no fixed onboard SPI device on
# this board - see eusci_b.py's own docstring). Not a byte-tap -> Event.
sysbus AddWatchpointHook 0x4000200E 4 Write "print('[SPI] TX byte=0x%X' % (value & 0xFF))"

# EUSCI_B1 CTLW0 write watchpoint, firing only when the real UCTXSTT bit
# (0x2) is set - direct proof i2cTask genuinely issued a START condition,
# not just that main() didn't hang.
sysbus AddWatchpointHook 0x40002400 4 Write "if value & 0x2: print('[I2C1] UCTXSTT START condition')"

# TIMER_A0 CCR1 write watchpoint - real, register-level proof pwmTask
# genuinely sweeps the real PWM duty-cycle register over time (this
# emulator has no live counter/waveform simulation - see timer_a.py's
# own docstring; the concrete proof is this register's own changing
# value, not a simulated analog signal).
sysbus AddWatchpointHook 0x40000014 4 Write "print('[PWM] TA0CCR1 duty=%d' % value)"

start
